# DevOps and SEO

Ship a fast, indexable expedition site. The current app is still the create-next-app scaffold; do not launch that metadata.

## Environments

- Local: `npm run dev`. MySQL via `DATABASE_URL` in an uncommitted `.env`.
- Production builds: `npm run build` then `npm start`. Prisma client must be generated before build. Apply migrations with `prisma migrate deploy`, never `migrate dev`, on production.
- Configure the host to bind as the platform requires. Do not commit machine-specific paths or secrets.

## Technical SEO

- Set `metadata` in the root layout: title template `%s · Ice Age Expeditions`, description about Himalayan 4x4 and motorbike expeditions, and `metadataBase` from the canonical site URL.
- Each expedition `generateMetadata` uses the route name, vehicle class, duration, and a unique description. Canonical path is `/expeditions/[slug]`.
- Add `app/sitemap.ts` for published expeditions, key guides (safety, gear, FAQ), and the homepage. Add `app/robots.ts` that allows public routes and disallows `/ops` and booking callbacks.
- Use one `h1` per page. Expedition pages: name plus region. Support copy with `TouristTrip`, `FAQPage`, `BreadcrumbList`, and `Organization` JSON-LD that matches visible content.
- Open Graph images should be route photography at 1200×630 with the expedition name burned in or composed, with a text alternative.

## Performance

- Hero images use `preload` only above the fold. Galleries lazy-load.
- Cache published catalog reads. Revalidate when ops publishes or closes a departure.
- Do not block the first expedition view on a client-side fetch of the same data.

## Launch checks

- `npm run lint` and `npm run build` succeed.
- Homepage title, sitemap, and robots are production copy.
- Draft expeditions and `/ops` are absent from the sitemap and carry `noindex` if they are reachable at all.
